L4.C1 ocean-wave-atmosphere coupled build
==========================================

This case builds the MITgcm component library and links it with the SKRIPS
ESMF coupler, WRF, and WAVEWATCH III (WW3). Building the executable and
running the Red Sea example are separate gates: the external runtime data are
not bundled completely in this source directory.

Build prerequisites
-------------------

Provide compatible, already-built installations of:

* ESMF and its ESMFMKFILE;
* WRF 4.7.1 with the SKRIPS ESMF overlays;
* WW3 6.07.1 with the SKRIPS WW3 overlays and all objects in model/obj;
* MITgcm checkpoint68r;
* MPI and NetCDF C/Fortran development files; and
* the L3.C1 case in this repository, which supplies common MITgcm sources and
  build utilities.

The installer checks the required environment variables and key generated
artifacts before it creates any build directories. At minimum, configure:

    export SKRIPS_DIR=/path/to/skrips
    export L3_CASE_DIR=$SKRIPS_DIR/coupler/L3.C1.coupled_RS2012_ring
    export WRF_DIR=/path/to/wrf-4.7.1-skrips-build
    export WW3_DIR=/path/to/ww3-6.07.1-skrips-build
    export MITGCM_DIR=/path/to/MITgcm-checkpoint68r
    export ESMF_DIR=/path/to/esmf
    export ESMFMKFILE=/path/to/esmf.mk

Also set ESMF_LIB, ESMF_MOD, ESMF_OS, ESMF_COMPILER, SKRIPS_MPI_INC,
SKRIPS_MPI_LIB, SKRIPS_NETCDF_INCLUDE, and SKRIPS_NETCDF_LIB consistently with
those installations.

Build
-----

For an interactive confirmation:

    ./install.sh

For an automated build after reviewing the exported paths:

    ./install.sh --yes

The installer deliberately refuses to reuse existing build/ or code/
directories. Use a fresh case copy for a clean rebuild. A successful build
produces:

    build/mitgcmuv
    build/mmout/mitgcm_org_ocn.mod
    build/mmout/libmitgcm_org_ocn.a
    build/mmout/libmitgcmrtl.a
    coupledCode/esmf_application

Runtime data gate
-----------------

The Red Sea runtime case is maintained separately at:

    https://github.com/iurnus/L4.C1.coupled_RS2012

Clone it with Git LFS enabled and verify that its LFS objects are materialized
before attempting runCase.init and runCase. A successful compile alone does
not assert that the external case data are complete or that a scientific
validation has passed.
